{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.AlternatingZetaTwo","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.AlternatingZetaTwo","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.ZetaValues"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_alternating_zeta_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_alternating_zeta_two","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/AlternatingZetaTwo.lean#L70-L92","doc":"**The alternating `ζ(2)`**: `Σ_{n≥1} (−1)^n/n² = −π²/12`, in the indexing the\ncorpus's `LiTwo` uses. Mathlib has `hasSum_zeta_two` but no alternating analogue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.summable_one_div_succ_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.summable_one_div_succ_sq","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/AlternatingZetaTwo.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_one_div_succ_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_one_div_succ_sq","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/AlternatingZetaTwo.lean#L44-L46","doc":"`Σ 1/(n+1)² = π²/6`, in shifted indexing — the summability workhorse. ","signatureChunk":0}]}